# CatNon School Helper

A lightweight, offline-capable PWA (Progressive Web App) for students. Stores all data locally on the device — no account or internet connection required after the first load.

---

## Files

| File | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `index.html` | Main app — all UI, logic, and styles in one file |
| `sw.js` | Service worker — enables offline use and asset caching |
| `manifest.json` | PWA manifest — allows "Add to Home Screen" on mobile |
| `icon.png` | App icon (512×512) |

---

## Features

### 📷 Pictures
- Organize photos into named albums
- Upload multiple photos at once (tap or drag & drop)
- Assign photos to albums on upload, or move them later
- Albums have a custom sort order (lower number = shown first)
- Uncategorized album collects any photos not assigned to a folder
- Tap any photo to open a full-screen lightbox
- Delete or move photos from the lightbox options menu

### 📝 Notes
- Create and edit freeform text notes
- Notes auto-save while typing (800ms debounce)
- Rename or delete notes from the gear icon on each card
- Notes are sorted by last modified date

### 🗺️ Backtracker
- Records your GPS path as a polyline on a live map (OpenStreetMap)
- Start / Stop tracking with one button
- Snap-to-location button recenters the map on your current position
- Reset button clears the recorded path
- Compass overlay shows device heading (requires device orientation permission on iOS)

---

## Data Storage

All data is stored in the browser's **IndexedDB** under the database `CatNonHelperDB`. Nothing is sent to any server.

| Store | Contents |
|-------|----------|
| `photos` | Photo entries with base64 image data, album assignment, and date |
| `albums` | Album names, sort order, and creation date |
| `notes` | Note title, body, and timestamps |

Current DB version: **4**

> Clearing browser site data or using a different browser will erase all stored content. There is no cloud backup.

---

## Offline Support

The service worker (`sw.js`) caches the app shell on first load, including:
- `index.html`
- `manifest.json`
- Leaflet map library (CSS + JS)
- Google Fonts

After the first visit the app works fully offline, except for map tiles (those require a connection to load new areas).

---

## Installation (Add to Home Screen)

**Android (Chrome):**
1. Open the app in Chrome
2. Tap the three-dot menu → "Add to Home screen"
3. Confirm — the app will appear as a standalone icon

**iOS (Safari):**
1. Open the app in Safari
2. Tap the Share button → "Add to Home Screen"
3. Confirm — the app opens without browser UI

---

## Browser Compatibility

Requires a modern browser with IndexedDB support. Chrome is recommended. Safari works but requires user permission for device orientation (compass feature).

---

## Known Limitations

- Photos are stored as base64 in IndexedDB — large photo libraries may hit browser storage limits
- Map tiles do not cache offline (only the map library itself is cached)
- No export or backup functionality
- Single-user, single-device only
